  "key_findings": [
    "All 10,496 routed experts fit in VRAM (18.7 GiB) on a 30 GB card - expert cache hit rate is 100%, nothing is streamed.",
    "A 256K context is NOT free on this card: KV cache (5 GiB) plus a 4096-token prompt batch pushed dedicated VRAM to 28.53 GB and spilled 3.24 GB into shared (GTT) memory, dropping prefill from ~1,220 to ~570 tok/s (a 2.2x loss).",
    "128K context with --prompt-batch 2048 keeps shared memory at 0.43 GB (no spill) and delivers ~1,220 tok/s prefill on a 42K-token prompt.",
    "Long-context slowdown beyond ~40K tokens is dominated by attention complexity, not by spilling: at 92K tokens prefill is ~694-707 tok/s even with zero spill.",
    "MTP speculative decoding works well on this model: draft acceptance is 70-93% on ordinary conversations, which is where the 128-176 tok/s decode comes from.",
    "The conversation cache stays off with 32 GB of RAM ('not enough free RAM to park conversations'). Multi-turn agent use re-prefills every turn."
